{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/atomic-structure/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/atomic-structure.html","area":"students","kind":"topic","title":"Atomic Structure | Chemistry Foundations","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"mb-4 flex items-center justify-between\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition flex items-center\">\n        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Foundations\n      </a>\n      <!-- Progress indicator -->\n      <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n        <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">\n          <span id=\"topic-progress-text\" data-bidemy=\"progress-text\">0% Complete</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"w-24 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full overflow-hidden\" data-bidemy=\"progress\">\n          <div id=\"topic-progress-bar\" class=\"h-full bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-400 to-indigo-500 transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -atom text-indigo-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"atom\">atom</span>Atomic Structure\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Understanding the structure of atoms, subatomic particles, isotopes, and electron configuration.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-indigo-50 border-l-4 border-indigo-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-indigo-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• Describe the structure of the atom</li>\n          <li>• Identify locations and properties of protons, neutrons, and electrons</li>\n          <li>• Define atomic number and mass number</li>\n          <li>• Explain isotopes and calculate relative atomic mass</li>\n          <li>• Write electron configurations for simple atoms</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: What is an Atom? -->\n      <section id=\"section-1\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          What is an Atom?\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\">An <strong class=\"text-indigo-600\">atom</strong> is the smallest particle of an element that can take part in a chemical reaction. The word \"atom\" comes from the Greek word \"atomos\" meaning indivisible.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-100 to-purple-100 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-800 font-medium text-center\">Atoms are incredibly small! A typical atom has a diameter of about 0.1 to 0.5 nanometers. If you could line up 10 million atoms side by side, they would only measure about 1 millimeter!</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: Subatomic Particles -->\n      <section id=\"section-2\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          Subatomic Particles\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Atoms consist of three main subatomic particles:</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"overflow-x-auto mb-4\">\n            <table class=\"w-full border-collapse border border-gray-300 rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm\">\n              <thead class=\"bg-indigo-600 text-white\">\n                <tr>\n                  <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Particle</th>\n                  <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Symbol</th>\n                  <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Relative Mass</th>\n                  <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Relative Charge</th>\n                  <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Location</th>\n                </tr>\n              </thead>\n              <tbody class=\"bg-white\">\n                <tr>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 font-medium\">Proton</td>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">p</td>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">1</td>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center text-red-600 font-bold\">+1</td>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Nucleus</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 font-medium\">Neutron</td>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">n</td>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">1</td>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">0</td>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Nucleus</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 font-medium\">Electron</td>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">e⁻</td>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">1/1840 ≈ 0</td>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center text-blue-600 font-bold\">−1</td>\n                  <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3\">Electron shells</td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Key Points</h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-yellow-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>• The <strong>nucleus</strong> contains protons and neutrons (most of the atom's mass)</li>\n              <li>• Electrons orbit the nucleus in electron shells (energy levels)</li>\n              <li>• An atom is neutral: number of protons = number of electrons</li>\n              <li>• Most of an atom is empty space!</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: Atomic Number & Mass Number -->\n      <section id=\"section-3\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Atomic Number and Mass Number\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\">Atomic Number (Z)</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">The number of protons in the nucleus. It identifies the element.</p>\n            <p class=\"mt-2 text-green-700 font-medium text-center\">Z = Number of Protons</p>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-purple-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\">Mass Number (A)</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">The total number of protons and neutrons in the nucleus.</p>\n            <p class=\"mt-2 text-purple-700 font-medium text-center\">A = Protons + Neutrons</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Nuclear Notation -->\n        <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3 text-center\">Nuclear Notation</h4>\n          <div class=\"flex items-center justify-center py-4\">\n            <div class=\"relative text-center mr-2\">\n              <span class=\"absolute -top-6 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 text-xs text-gray-500\">A</span>\n              <span class=\"absolute -bottom-5 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 text-xs text-gray-500\">Z</span>\n              <div class=\"text-xl\">\n                <sup class=\"text-indigo-600 font-bold\">23</sup><br>\n                <sub class=\"text-gray-500\">11</sub>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <span class=\"text-2xl font-bold\">Na</span>\n            <span class=\"ml-3 text-gray-600\">→ Sodium atom</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-center text-sm text-gray-600 mt-6\">Sodium has 11 protons, 11 electrons, and 23 − 11 = <strong>12 neutrons</strong></p>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-indigo-50 text-left font-semibold text-indigo-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-indigo-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-indigo-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Worked Example: Finding Particles</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">An atom has atomic number 17 and mass number 35. How many protons, neutrons, and electrons does it have?</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-indigo-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Find protons</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-indigo-700 mt-1\">Protons = Atomic number = <strong>17</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Find electrons (atom is neutral)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 mt-1\">Electrons = Protons = <strong>17</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Find neutrons</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 mt-1\">Neutrons = Mass number − Atomic number</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700\">Neutrons = 35 − 17 = <strong>18</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Answer: 17 protons, 17 electrons, 18 neutrons (Chlorine-35)</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Isotopes -->\n      <section id=\"section-4\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Isotopes\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\"><strong class=\"text-indigo-600\">Isotopes</strong> are atoms of the same element with the same number of protons but different numbers of neutrons. They have the same atomic number but different mass numbers.</p>\n          \n          <!-- Isotopes Example -->\n          <div class=\"bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-3 text-center\">Example: Isotopes of Carbon</h4>\n            <div class=\"grid grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-center\">\n              <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg shadow\">\n                <div class=\"font-bold text-lg\">Carbon-12</div>\n                <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">⁶⁄₆C</div>\n                <div class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1\">6p, 6n, 6e</div>\n                <div class=\"text-xs text-green-600 mt-1\">Most common (98.9%)</div>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg shadow\">\n                <div class=\"font-bold text-lg\">Carbon-13</div>\n                <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">¹³⁄₆C</div>\n                <div class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1\">6p, 7n, 6e</div>\n                <div class=\"text-xs text-yellow-600 mt-1\">Rare (1.1%)</div>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg shadow\">\n                <div class=\"font-bold text-lg\">Carbon-14</div>\n                <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">¹⁴⁄₆C</div>\n                <div class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1\">6p, 8n, 6e</div>\n                <div class=\"text-xs text-red-600 mt-1\">Radioactive</div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Relative Atomic Mass -->\n        <div class=\"bg-teal-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-teal-200 mb-4\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-teal-800 mb-2\">Relative Atomic Mass (Aᵣ)</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2\">The weighted average mass of all naturally occurring isotopes:</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded font-mono text-center\">\n            Aᵣ = Σ (isotope mass × % abundance) / 100\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-teal-50 text-left font-semibold text-teal-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-teal-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-teal-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Worked Example: Calculating Relative Atomic Mass</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Chlorine has two isotopes: ³⁵Cl (75%) and ³⁷Cl (25%). Calculate the relative atomic mass.</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-teal-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Formula:</strong> Aᵣ = Σ (mass × %)/100</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Substitute:</strong></p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 mt-1\">Aᵣ = (35 × 75 + 37 × 25) / 100</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700\">Aᵣ = (2625 + 925) / 100</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700\">Aᵣ = 3550 / 100</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Answer: Aᵣ = 35.5</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Electron Configuration -->\n      <section id=\"section-5\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n          Electron Configuration\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Electrons are arranged in energy levels (shells) around the nucleus. The maximum electrons in each shell follow the formula <strong class=\"text-indigo-600\">2n²</strong>.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"grid grid-cols-4 gap-2 text-center mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded shadow\">\n              <div class=\"font-bold text-indigo-600\">1st Shell</div>\n              <div class=\"text-2xl font-bold\">2</div>\n              <div class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">2(1)² = 2</div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded shadow\">\n              <div class=\"font-bold text-indigo-600\">2nd Shell</div>\n              <div class=\"text-2xl font-bold\">8</div>\n              <div class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">2(2)² = 8</div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded shadow\">\n              <div class=\"font-bold text-indigo-600\">3rd Shell</div>\n              <div class=\"text-2xl font-bold\">18</div>\n              <div class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">2(3)² = 18</div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded shadow\">\n              <div class=\"font-bold text-indigo-600\">4th Shell</div>\n              <div class=\"text-2xl font-bold\">32</div>\n              <div class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">2(4)² = 32</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-3 rounded-r-lg mb-4\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\"><strong>Note:</strong> For the first 20 elements, the 3rd shell fills to 8 electrons before the 4th shell starts (due to subshell ordering).</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Electron Configuration Table -->\n        <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 overflow-x-auto\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3\">Electron Configurations of First 20 Elements</h4>\n          <table class=\"w-full text-sm\">\n            <thead class=\"bg-indigo-600 text-white\">\n              <tr>\n                <th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Element</th>\n                <th class=\"p-2\">Symbol</th>\n                <th class=\"p-2\">Z</th>\n                <th class=\"p-2\">1st</th>\n                <th class=\"p-2\">2nd</th>\n                <th class=\"p-2\">3rd</th>\n                <th class=\"p-2\">4th</th>\n                <th class=\"p-2\">Notation</th>\n              </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody class=\"bg-white\">\n              <tr><td class=\"p-2 border\">Hydrogen</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">H</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">1</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">1</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border font-mono\">1</td></tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\"><td class=\"p-2 border\">Helium</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">He</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">2</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">2</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border font-mono\">2</td></tr>\n              <tr><td class=\"p-2 border\">Lithium</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">Li</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">3</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">2</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">1</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border font-mono\">2,1</td></tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\"><td class=\"p-2 border\">Carbon</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">C</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">6</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">2</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">4</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border font-mono\">2,4</td></tr>\n              <tr><td class=\"p-2 border\">Neon</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">Ne</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">10</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">2</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">8</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border font-mono\">2,8</td></tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\"><td class=\"p-2 border\">Sodium</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">Na</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">11</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">2</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">8</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">1</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border font-mono\">2,8,1</td></tr>\n              <tr><td class=\"p-2 border\">Chlorine</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">Cl</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">17</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">2</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">8</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">7</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border font-mono\">2,8,7</td></tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\"><td class=\"p-2 border\">Argon</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">Ar</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">18</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">2</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">8</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">8</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">-</td><td class=\"p-2 border font-mono\">2,8,8</td></tr>\n              <tr><td class=\"p-2 border\">Potassium</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">K</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">19</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">2</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">8</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">8</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">1</td><td class=\"p-2 border font-mono\">2,8,8,1</td></tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\"><td class=\"p-2 border\">Calcium</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">Ca</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">20</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">2</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">8</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">8</td><td class=\"p-2 border text-center\">2</td><td class=\"p-2 border font-mono\">2,8,8,2</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 6: Atomic Models -->\n      <section id=\"section-6\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">6</span>\n          Historical Development of Atomic Models\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n          <!-- Dalton -->\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-gray-50 text-left font-semibold text-gray-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-gray-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -circle text-gray-400 mr-2\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>Dalton's Solid Sphere (1803)</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-4\">\n                <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">Dalton proposed that all matter is made of tiny, solid, indestructible spheres called atoms.</p>\n                <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                  <li>• Atoms are solid, indivisible spheres</li>\n                  <li>• All atoms of an element are identical</li>\n                  <li>• Atoms combine in simple whole number ratios</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          \n          <!-- Thomson -->\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-purple-50 text-left font-semibold text-purple-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-purple-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -circle text-purple-400 mr-2\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>Thomson's Plum Pudding (1897)</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-4\">\n                <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">After discovering the electron, Thomson proposed atoms are positive spheres with negative electrons embedded throughout.</p>\n                <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                  <li>• Atoms contain smaller particles (electrons)</li>\n                  <li>• Atoms are divisible</li>\n                  <li>• Positive charge spread throughout</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          \n          <!-- Rutherford -->\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-green-50 text-left font-semibold text-green-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-green-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -circle text-green-400 mr-2\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>Rutherford's Nuclear Model (1911)</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-4\">\n                <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">Through his gold foil experiment, Rutherford discovered atoms have a small, dense, positively charged nucleus.</p>\n                <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                  <li>• Most of the atom is empty space</li>\n                  <li>• Positive charge concentrated in tiny nucleus</li>\n                  <li>• Electrons orbit the nucleus</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          \n          <!-- Bohr -->\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-blue-50 text-left font-semibold text-blue-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-blue-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -circle text-blue-400 mr-2\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>Bohr's Model (1913)</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-4\">\n                <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">Bohr proposed that electrons orbit the nucleus in fixed energy levels and can jump between levels by absorbing or emitting energy.</p>\n                <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                  <li>• Electrons in fixed orbits (energy levels)</li>\n                  <li>• Each orbit has specific energy</li>\n                  <li>• Electrons can jump between levels</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 7: Practice Problems -->\n      <section id=\"section-7\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-indigo-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. An atom has 17 protons and 18 neutrons. What is its atomic number and mass number?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Atomic number = 17 (number of protons)</p>\n                <p>Mass number = 17 + 18 = <strong>35</strong></p>\n                <p>This is chlorine-35.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. Write the electron configuration for phosphorus (Z = 15).</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Phosphorus has 15 electrons.</p>\n                <p>Configuration: <strong>2, 8, 5</strong></p>\n                <p>First shell: 2, Second shell: 8, Third shell: 5</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. An ion has 12 protons, 14 neutrons, and 10 electrons. What is its symbol and charge?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Z = 12 → Magnesium (Mg)</p>\n                <p>Charge = +12 + (-10) = +2</p>\n                <p><strong>Mg²⁺</strong> (Magnesium ion)</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. Copper has isotopes ⁶³Cu (69.2%) and ⁶⁵Cu (30.8%). Calculate Aᵣ.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Aᵣ = (63 × 69.2 + 65 × 30.8) / 100</p>\n                <p>Aᵣ = (4359.6 + 2002) / 100 = 63.6</p>\n                <p><strong>Aᵣ = 63.6</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n      <section id=\"section-8\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-indigo-50 to-purple-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-indigo-200\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways for WAEC/JAMB/NECO</h3>\n          <ul class=\"text-indigo-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n            <li>• Know properties of protons, neutrons, and electrons (mass, charge, location)</li>\n            <li>• Calculate particles from atomic and mass numbers</li>\n            <li>• Understand isotopes and calculate relative atomic mass</li>\n            <li>• Write electron configurations for first 20 elements</li>\n            <li>• Know the historical development of atomic models</li>\n            <li>• Remember: A = Z + N (Mass = Protons + Neutrons)</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Complete Topic Button -->\n      <div class=\"mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200\">\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Ready to Complete?</h3>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">View all sections, then take the quiz to mark this topic as complete.</p>\n          </div>\n          <button id=\"topic-complete-btn\" disabled=\"\" class=\"px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gray-300 text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed opacity-50 flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-medium\">\n            <span class=\"mi -lock mr-2\" data-mi=\"lock\">lock</span>\n            <span>Complete (0% viewed)</span>\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n  <!-- Topic Tracking and Quiz System -->\n  \n\n\n<div data-bidemy=\"quiz\"></div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-indigo-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n    .content-card {\n      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);\n      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n    }\n    .accordion-content {\n      max-height: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      transition: max-height 0.3s ease-out;\n    }\n    .accordion-content.open {\n      max-height: 2000px;\n    }\n    .step-card {\n      transition: all 0.2s ease;\n    }\n    .step-card:hover {\n      transform: translateX(4px);\n    }\n    #topic-complete-btn {\n      transition: all 0.3s ease;\n    }\n    #topic-complete-btn:not(:disabled):hover {\n      transform: scale(1.02);\n    }"],"quiz":{"topicId":"atomic-structure","subject":"chemistry","passingScore":60,"questions":[{"question":"What is the relative charge of a proton?","options":["-1","0","+1","+2"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A proton has a relative charge of +1. Electrons have -1, neutrons have 0."},{"question":"Where are protons and neutrons located in an atom?","options":["In the electron shells","In the nucleus","Orbiting the nucleus","In the protons"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Protons and neutrons are found in the nucleus (center) of the atom."},{"question":"What does the atomic number represent?","options":["Number of neutrons","Number of protons","Total mass of the atom","Number of electrons in outer shell"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Atomic number (Z) = number of protons in the nucleus."},{"question":"An atom has atomic number 11 and mass number 23. How many neutrons does it have?","options":["11","12","23","34"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Neutrons = Mass number - Atomic number = 23 - 11 = 12 neutrons."},{"question":"What are isotopes?","options":["Atoms with different numbers of protons","Atoms with the same number of protons but different neutrons","Atoms with the same mass number","Charged atoms"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Isotopes are atoms of the same element (same Z) with different mass numbers (different N)."},{"question":"What is the electron configuration of chlorine (Z = 17)?","options":["2,8,7","2,8,8","2,8,6,1","2,8,5,2"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Chlorine has 17 electrons: 2 in first shell, 8 in second, 7 in third = 2,8,7"},{"question":"The relative atomic mass of chlorine is 35.5. Why isn't it a whole number?","options":["Chlorine atoms have fractional masses","It's an average of isotopes","Electrons add to the mass","Neutrons have variable mass"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The 35.5 is a weighted average of chlorine-35 (75%) and chlorine-37 (25%) isotopes."},{"question":"Who proposed the nuclear model of the atom after the gold foil experiment?","options":["John Dalton","J.J. Thomson","Ernest Rutherford","Niels Bohr"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Rutherford discovered the nucleus through his gold foil experiment in 1911."}]},"tracker":{"topicId":"atomic-structure","topicTitle":"Atomic Structure","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6","section-7","section-8"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}